When you are made redundant in Australia, part of your payout may be **tax-free** under the ATO's genuine redundancy provisions. For FY2025-26, the tax-free threshold is **$12,524 (base amount) plus $6,264 for each completed year of service**. An employee with 10 years of service has a tax-free threshold of $75,164. Any redundancy payment above this amount is classified as an Employment Termination Payment (ETP) and taxed at concessional rates — up to 30% for employees under 65, rather than the standard marginal rate of up to 47%.

The Fair Work Act sets minimum redundancy pay based on years of service, ranging from 4 weeks' pay (1–2 years) to 16 weeks' pay (9+ years). Many employers, particularly larger organisations and those under enterprise agreements, pay above these minimums. Employees at or above the normal retirement age of 67 do not qualify for the tax-free genuine redundancy threshold — the entire payment is treated as an ETP. This calculator uses the 2025-26 ATO thresholds and ETP concessional rates to estimate your after-tax payout.
